{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LRimYoPEvyhX44xehbupvd","type":"tool_result","content":"180\t         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n181\t         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n182\t         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n183\t    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n184\t         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n185\t         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n186\t         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n187\t         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n188\t         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n189\t    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n190\t         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n191\t         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n192\t         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n193\t         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n194\t         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n195\t         no suppression list in this file.\n196\t  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n197\t    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n198\t         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n199\t         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n200\t         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n201\t         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n202\t         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n203\t         passes.\n204\t    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n205\t         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n206\t         registered by the permanent detector\").\n207\t\n208\tStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n209\t\"\"\"\n210\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n211\t\n212\timport argparse\n213\timport glob\n214\timport json\n215\timport os\n216\timport re\n217\timport sys\n218\timport time\n219\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n220\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n221\tfrom pathlib import Path\n222\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n223\t\n224\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n225\t# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n226\t# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n227\t# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n228\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n230\t_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n231\t_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n232\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n233\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n234\t\n235\ttry:\n236\t    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\n237\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n238\t    _rp = None\n239\t\n240\t\n241\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n242\t# Pricing tables\n243\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n247\t# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\n248\tfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n249\t\n250\t_install_parts(globals(), (\n251\t    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n252\t))\n253\t\n254\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n255\t    sys.exit(main())\n256\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c0bb90c-7d31-4674-a599-70c9f0a2963d","uuid":"3628ad5c-f949-4d32-b6e1-d37042ce67e1","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:17:48.856Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py","content":"         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n         no suppression list in this file.\n  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n         passes.\n    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n         registered by the permanent detector\").\n\nStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport glob\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n\ntry:\n    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n    _rp = None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Pricing tables\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\nfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n\n_install_parts(globals(), (\n    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":77,"startLine":180,"totalLines":256}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LRimYoPEvyhX44xehbupvd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
