{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ofB8u2tHAxJHbztvmuVmz","type":"tool_result","content":"276:- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n277-  there is left out.\n278:- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n279:  - checks every archive member before extraction (`_restore_archive.py`):\n280-    no links, no absolute paths, no `..`, no name outside the layout, and\n281-    never `audit-key` or `.salt`, in any letter case;\n282-  - resolves `--dest` physically and refuses a link, or a file, as the\n283-    destination;\n284-  - refuses a restore target that is a link or sits under one;\n285-  - runs the same checks in the preview and in the apply.\n286-- On macOS, the system `tar` adds a hidden AppleDouble member\n287-  (`._<name>`) for each file or folder with extended attributes, and\n288:  `ceo-restore.sh` refused every such archive (`archive refused path:\n289:  ._.`). `ceo-backup.sh` no longer writes these members. For archives\n290-  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n291-  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n292-  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n293-  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n294-  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n295-  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n296-- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n297-  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n298-  `--apply` restores.\n299-\n300-### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n301-\n--\n344:  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n345:  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n346:  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n347-\n348-### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n349-\n350-- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n351-  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n352-  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n353-- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n354-  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n355-  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n356-- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n357-  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n358-- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n--\n458:  scheduled backup with `ceo-backup.sh`.\n459-\n460-### What an adopter should know before installing or upgrading\n461-\n462-- Coming from v1.4.2, read `[1.4.3]` too. Its notes apply.\n463-- The requirements are unchanged: Claude Code 2.1.280 or later, Python 3.9\n464-  or later, and Node.js 20 or later for the npm shim.\n465-- A command that reaches `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard` or a forced\n466-  `git push` indirectly may now be blocked, and so may a shell body the\n467-  guard cannot parse. To turn the scan off, set\n468-  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0`, or only the heuristics with\n469-  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0`, in the environment Claude Code starts\n470-  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n--\n481:- `ceo-restore.sh` previews by default; pass `--apply` to restore. Keep your\n482-  own copy of `audit-key` and `.salt`, because the backup leaves them out.\n483-- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 60]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c0bb90c-7d31-4674-a599-70c9f0a2963d","uuid":"da1952ca-1fdf-4224-8dbe-0271a0a43ff3","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:23:42.036Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"276:- `ceo-backup.sh` archives only the regular files of `memory/`; a link\n277-  there is left out.\n278:- `ceo-restore.sh`:\n279:  - checks every archive me